{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>For you went up onto your father's bed.</b> You went up onto his bed — and when? At the time of the mandrakes, as it is said there: ״therefore he shall lie with you tonight instead of your son's mandrakes.״" "<b>You defiled my couch — he went up.</b> Let him be removed until Moses comes, upon him be peace, for it is said of him: ״ומשה עלה״, and he shall bring you near, as it is said: ״Let Reuben live and not die.״ Another interpretation: אז חללת יצועי עלה — you defiled my couch that was elevated more than those of my fathers, in which there was a flaw, but in my couch no flaw was found, and you defiled it. Another interpretation: חללת יצועי עלה — you defiled him who went up onto my couch, that is, your father this one; and just as he said משכבי אביך speaking of another, so he said יצועי עלה speaking of another."], :book :genesis, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 49, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:07:21.833764152Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}